N1  - <p>BOINC criterion evidence - Acknowledgments, verbatim: "This research was made possible by processor time donated by the distributed computing community and some experiments presented in this paper were carried out using the Grid'5000 testbed." Section III-A, verbatim: "the overall search algorithm was distributed using an island based coevolutionary model... A grid of up to 150 workstations was used." Section IV-C, verbatim: "The computational cost for the synthesis of the circuits presented varied from a couple of hours on a single 2.8Ghz processor to a couple of weeks on 150 2.8Ghz processors." Section IV-C: "running the distributed evolutionary algorithm." Reference [1]: "Distributed hardware evolution project. http://dhep.ga." Listed on the BOINC publications page under Distributed Hardware Evolution Project. | Full text: arXiv:1901.07023 (2019) | Link: DHEP / BOINC | Source: arXiv (2019)ER&nbsp;&nbsp;-</p>
